  "reason": "The best current result is RNA-only multiprofile PCA with avgpool (0.591 acc / 0.573 F1), while image-only ResNet single is weak (0.208 acc / 0.172 F1). It is unclear whether the multiprofile avgpool gain is specific to RNA or whether image can provide useful signal under the same profile/aggregation setting. config_011 tests image-only ResNet with multiprofile avgpool, isolating the profile/aggregation effect for the image modality before introducing fusion. This is a simple, controlled extension of the promising setting and reduces uncertainty about whether image is worth including in later multimodal experiments, making it a high-information use of the next budget."
